@ProjectManager please freeze those roles in http://sharepoint/treasury_management_system_implementation/production_deployment_readiness_spec today, and let’s confirm who signs if backup is unavailable.

I’m aligned with that blocker split, and it feels like the cleanest way to keep July 18 realistic.  
Should I be worried that “posting timing” is still being treated as a design detail somewhere, when it can break reconciliation and Finance ops?  

@Architecture, please mark blocker vs overhead in http://sharepoint/treasury_management_system_implementation/risk:_vendor_integration_complexity_spec by Friday, and @Vendor please include test impacts plus any data-mapping gaps for each blocker path. If we can lock that on a yes/no basis, I think we can avoid dragging Security and reporting into another rework loop.

I think Ops can publish the table Friday, but migration should stay provisional until more layered cases are reviewed.  
@Operations please include owner, evidence, hard-stop/remediation, `branch tag required`, and 2–3 tagged migration examples in http://sharepoint/aml_(anti-money_laundering)_project/risk:_inconsistent_kyc_records_spec.  
