If any item changes thresholds or escalation, can we keep it as blocker and lock the rest against http://sharepoint/aml_(anti-money_laundering)_project/risk:_incomplete_regulatory_coverage_spec?

Locked for me too, with one gap: who signs off on the provisional migration row if layered cases stay thin?  
@Ops please publish Friday with owner, evidence, hard-stop/remediation, `branch tag required`, and migration cleanup named in-row.  
@Compliance can you confirm whether provisional wording is enough, or do you want a formal hold in http://sharepoint/aml_(anti-money_laundering)_project/risk:_inconsistent_kyc_records_spec?

Not to be that person, but I’d freeze CIDRs after Friday’s bank-gateway test.  
In Project Meridian, locking them earlier made Security reopen the allowlist twice.  
@Vendor, please post endpoint, cadence, and named owner in the spec by July 16.

